00:00:09.667 --> 00:00:10.500
"Someone."

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.550
Like, he's so talented.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:12.450
So how did y'all meet?

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:14.100
Was it while you were
working, like in the studio?

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.030
- Yeah, well, yes.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.490
So we got set up, we are both at RCA.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:20.910
And we got set up by our A&amp;R person there,

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:23.896
just not set up like that,
but just set up to work.

00:00:23.896 --> 00:00:24.729
- Yeah.

00:00:24.729 --> 00:00:26.610
- And I was like cutting
a couple of the songs

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.376
that he had written.

00:00:28.376 --> 00:00:30.150
- So good.
- And we met at Aroma Cafe

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:31.800
on Tujunga, in the Valley.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.780
And then we ended up being there
for like two hours talking.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.490
And I was like, "(gasps) I gotta go.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:36.323
What am I doing?

00:00:36.323 --> 00:00:38.850
Why are we talking about
all these like '90s music

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.890
that we like and like
really connecting and-"

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:42.420
- Because you're cool
and 90s music is awesome.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:43.253
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:43.253 --> 00:00:45.147
- So that's how we met.

00:00:45.147 --> 00:00:47.520
And then we recorded a
little bit in the studio

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:49.860
and everything was pretty professional.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.240
And then he asked me out on a date,

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.830
it was around Valentine's Day.

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:55.620
And then we like casually,
kind of started dating

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:56.970
like a month after that.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:59.700
And we broke up and then
we got back together

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.350
and then we broke up and
then we got back together.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:02.297
- Oh you did?
- And we were like,

00:01:02.297 --> 00:01:03.171
"we shoulda have a baby."

00:01:03.171 --> 00:01:04.004
- Oh! (laughing)
- And then we had a baby

00:01:04.004 --> 00:01:05.063
and I was like, "if any
of my kids not do that,

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:07.173
you're all gonna die."

00:01:07.173 --> 00:01:08.370
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:09.848
But it worked out really great for us.

00:01:09.848 --> 00:01:11.580
- Oh my god, I love this story.

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:12.525
This is a movie.

00:01:12.525 --> 00:01:13.810
You should produce this movie
- And like two weeks later,

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:14.850
I was pregnant.

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:16.410
- Oh my gosh.
- I know.

00:01:16.410 --> 00:01:17.332
I know, naughty.

00:01:17.332 --> 00:01:19.514
- But he's so funny.

00:01:19.514 --> 00:01:20.760
- He's so funny.
- He's so funny.

00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:21.690
I mean, here's the thing,

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:24.270
I feel like if someone can make you laugh.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:25.103
- [Hillary] I know.

00:01:25.103 --> 00:01:26.610
- Like, you know what
I'm saying, love changes,

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:28.710
